  "headline": {
    "high_velocity_systems": "CONSISTENT with large margin. At v = 500 km/s the framework gives 0.009644 cm2/g, i.e. 64x below the MACS J0138 ceiling (0.613) and 21x below the DESI BAO ceiling (0.2). sigma/m falls with velocity, so the agreement only strengthens at the true v_pair ~ 2090 km/s.",
    "dwarf_velocity_systems": "VIOLATED against Horigome+ 2025: the framework is 31.4x above their 0.8 cm2/g 95% ceiling at v = 3 km/s and 3.08x above it at v = 10 km/s (2.465 cm2/g).",
    "published_dwarf_data_conflict": "The two published dwarf conditions bracket sigma/m(10 km/s) in opposite directions: Horigome+ 2025 requires < 0.8 cm2/g while Gilman+ 2026 disfavours < 10 cm2/g, a 12.5x contradiction. No single value \u2014 this framework's 2.465 included \u2014 can satisfy both.",
    "cloud9_velocity": "At v = 28 km/s the framework gives 100 cm2/g effective (177.8 total). Gilman+ 2023 begin to disfavor > 100 cm2/g below 30 km/s (ratio 1.0004). Ohana+ 2026's published Cloud-9 optimum is ~200 cm2/g, so the framework is 2.00x below it on the effective convention and 1.13x below it on the total convention (the paper's tau = 0.18 fiducial infers 483 cm2/g).",
